# Shell hooks stay LF regardless of core.autocrlf (which is `true` on the box this
# was written on, so a fresh clone would otherwise get CRLF here).
#
# Measured before adding this, rather than assumed: a CRLF copy of
# .githooks/pre-commit runs correctly under Git for Windows' sh -- it blocked a
# staged .dll with exit 1 and passed a clean tree with exit 0. So this is
# belt-and-braces for a clone on Linux or macOS, not a fix for a proven break.
.githooks/** text eol=lf
